<title>UK: Algerian Sonatrach cuts May LPG to $165/$170 a ton.</title>
<headline>Algerian Sonatrach cuts May LPG to $165/$170 a ton.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algerian state oil and gas company Sonatrach has announced its official posted prices for Liquefied Petroleum Gas (LPG) for May.</p>
<p>Propane has been set at $165 a tonne fob Bethioua, down by $10 a tonne from April.</p>
<p>Butane has been set at $170 a tonne fob Bethioua, also down by $10 a tonne from last month.</p>
<p>The premium for loading at Arzew or Skikda is $7 a tonne.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
